# Copy to .env and adjust: cp .env.example .env
# Used by `go run ./cmd/novil` (from apps/backend) and by docker compose.
# Variables already set in the environment take precedence over this file.

# The first admin, created on the first start when there are no users yet.
# Ignored afterwards. Like every new user, they must change the password
# after logging in.
NOVIL_ADMIN_USER=admin
NOVIL_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-please

# Secret that signs the login tokens (JWTs), at least 32 characters.
# Leave empty to have one generated and stored in <data dir>/jwt.key.
# Generate one with: openssl rand -hex 32
# Changing it logs everyone out.
NOVIL_JWT_SECRET=

# Comma-separated browser origins allowed to call the API (CORS), e.g. the
# Vite dev server. Mobile apps don't need an entry.
NOVIL_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# Each IP may try 5 passwords (login or password change) at once, then one
# more every 12 seconds. Behind a reverse proxy (nginx, Traefik, Caddy...)
# every request comes from the proxy's IP, so list the proxy here: its
# X-Forwarded-For header then tells the real client IP. IPs or CIDR ranges,
# comma-separated, e.g. 172.16.0.0/12 for a proxy in another Docker container.
# Only list proxies you run; anyone else could fake the header.
NOVIL_TRUSTED_PROXIES=

# Book requests look ISBNs up in Open Library and Google Books. Google works
# without a key, but then shares a small daily quota with everyone; a free
# key from https://console.cloud.google.com (Books API) makes it reliable.
NOVIL_GOOGLE_BOOKS_KEY=

# Leave NOVIL_ADDR and NOVIL_DATA_DIR unset unless you need to: the defaults
# (:8080 and ./data) suit local development, and in Docker the image sets
# NOVIL_DATA_DIR=/config, which a value here would override.
# NOVIL_ADDR=:8080
# NOVIL_DATA_DIR=data
